 "Beyond Suite Hotel Bangkok",
 "Beyond the beaches, Samui has the landmark Big Buddha at Wat Phra Yai, the Hin Ta Hin Yai rocks at Lamai, Wat Khunaram with the mummified body of Luang Pho Daeng, the Na Muang waterfalls in the middle of the island, and Bophut fishing village, which has turned into a seaside strip for eating and shopping. If you want to take a boat out snorkelling, Ang Thong Marine Park is one of the prettier day trips. Samui works for beach-goers, party people, families, and honeymooners alike.",
 "Beyond the ruins, Ayutthaya is known for food that goes with the town — boat noodles, roti sai mai, and big river prawns by the water. In the late afternoon, stop by a floating market or take a boat to see the temples around the island. End the day watching the temples lit up after dark, which has its own kind of beauty.",
 "Beyond the sea, the town itself has an old quarter along Bang Phra Canal, a morning market, and old Chinese shrines to wander. Down south there are small beaches around Khlong Yai and the Ban Hat Lek border market next to Cambodia. When fruit season comes around April to June, the orchards here produce durian, rambutan, and mangosteen just like the neighbouring provinces. If you like a quiet sea without the crowds, Trat is the kind of destination plenty of people travel a long way to reach.",
 "Beyond the tourist restaurants, Pattaya still has made-to-order shops, noodle stalls, and rice-and-curry joints at local prices tucked down the side streets — bold flavors and good value.",
