 "People come to Phuket to laze on the sand, take boats out to the Phi Phi Islands and Phang Nga Bay, head up to pay respects at the Big Buddha on Nakkerd Hill, and eat local Hokkien dishes like Hokkien mee and oh tao in the old town. It's a coastal province where beaches, islands, and old Chinese culture all mix together.",
 "People like to drive down for the seafood, pick up shrimp paste and fish sauce to take home, then catch a boat out to Koh Samet to laze on the sand. If you want an easy trip, wander the Yom Chinda old town, try some noodles, stop at a cafe, and carry on to the coast at Ban Phe or the river mouth at Pak Nam Prasae.",
 "People visiting Bangkok tend to pack a lot into one day — temples, markets, cafes, and rooftop bars — because the food and sights sit close together and link up easily by skytrain and boat.",
