 "Phetchabun in 1 Day Khao Kho & Wat Pha Sorn Kaew Highlights",
 "Phetchabun is where people from Bangkok and the central plains like to drive up for cool weather as the rainy season turns to winter. The province sits in a valley ringed by mountains, with Khao Kho and Phu Tab Berk where an early start often gets you a sea of mist. Up on Phu Tab",
 "Phetchabun is where people from Bangkok and the central plains like to drive up for cool weather as the rainy season turns to winter. The province sits in a valley ringed by mountains, with Khao Kho and Phu Tab Berk where an early start often gets you a sea of mist. Up on Phu Tab Berk there are cabbage fields stepping down the slopes and Hmong villages to stop at. If you're into history, the ancient town of Si Thep was just listed as a World Heritage Site. The food to take home is the sweet tamarind and sweet corn grown all over the province. One trip to Phetchabun gives you mountains, temples, and a car full of things to bring back.",
