 "The Inn Saladaeng",
 "The in-town markets have rice-and-curry plates, local sweets, and cheap breakfast bites to graze on.",
 "The island has coffee cafes, smoothies, and small dessert shops for a midday break — some with a sea view right on the beach.",
 "The island has little cafes serving fresh coffee and desserts dotted along the beaches and villages — a good place to pause for a coffee during the day.",
 "The island has plenty of vegan spots, smoothie bowls, and clean eating to suit the wellness and detox crowd staying long-term.",
 "The island has several beaches to choose from. Tawaen is the main, busiest beach, with the full range of water sports — parasailing, banana boats, and snorkeling. Samae and Nuan are quieter with clear water and are good for lazing around, while Tien is a calmer beach on the other side. If you want to stay over, there are places to sleep and seafood restaurants on the island. Koh Larn works for swimmers, water-sports fans, and anyone who just wants to relax by the beach. Honesty: it gets very crowded on holidays and the boats are packed, so go early; check the price and safety of water sports before you ride; the sea is murky on some days depending on the weather; and help keep the beaches clean by taking your trash back with you.",
 "The island has small cafes serving fresh coffee and desserts scattered along the beaches — a good place to stop and rest while cycling around.",
 "The island is flat, so it's easy to cycle past coconut groves, rubber plantation",
 "The island off Ban Phe, with clear water and white sand a short",
 "The island off Ban Phe, with clear water and white sand a short boat ride away. There's Sai Kaew Beach, Ao Phrao, and smaller coves to choose from for a stay",
 "The island off Pattaya, a short boat ride out — clear water, whi",
 "The island off Pattaya, a short boat ride out — clear water, white sand, good for swimming and snorkeling on a day trip",
 "The island off Pattaya — clear water and white sand, a boat ride out to swim and",
 "The island's busiest beach and main tourist area, with hotels, r",
 "The island's busiest beach and main tourist area, with hotels, restaurants, and",
 "The island's busiest beach and main tourist area, with hotels, restaurants, and Bangla Road buzzing at night. This is where the most foreign visitors gather.",
