 "The morning market has local eats and fruit, while the weekend walking street has street food, traditional sweets, and grilled seafood to graze on.",
 "The morning market has sticky rice, nam phrik, local vegetables, and regional sweets to graze on",
 "The MuG Resort",
 "The Na Ban pier area and Tawaen Beach have cafes, dessert shops, and snacks to drop by — while you wait for the boat or take a break from swimming.",
 "The Naklua area has markets and seafood restaurants with fresh catch at fair prices — prawns, shellfish, crab, and fish cooked fresh by the sea. This is where Pattaya locals actually go for seafood.",
 "The night market around Lee Gardens and Greenway brings together",
 "The night market around Lee Gardens and Greenway brings together street food, snacks, and shopping, open late — it's the city's after-dark eating and drinking quarter.",
 "The night market in the center of town brings together street food, grilled seafood, barbecue, and snacks. It's lively every night and easy on the wallet.",
 "The night market in the heart of Hua Hin sells grilled seafood, pad thai, fried snacks, and desserts. You can graze stall to stall all night.",
 "The night market in the Thong Sala pier area gathers Thai and southern street food, grilled and fried dishes, sweets, and fruit, at friendlier prices than the tourist beaches.",
 "The night markets around Lamai and Chaweng bring together Thai street food, grilled and fried snacks, and casual bites at friendlier prices than the resort restaurants.",
 "The north and west of the island are calm and quiet, with white-sand beaches like Bottle Beach (reachable only by boat), Koh Ma off Mae Haad where you can snorkel over coral, and Than Sadet waterfall inside the national park, once visited by Thai kings. The Srithanu area has become a hub for yoga, wellness, and health cafes where people stay for weeks. Thong Sala is the island's main pier and market town. You can come to Phangan to party, to find quiet, or to rest and recharge.",
 "The northern end, next to Phetchaburi, has palm groves and palm-sugar sweets, including mor kaeng custard, thong yot, and fresh toddy palm fruit in season.",
 "The north of the province has Khao Lak and Takua Pa, the launch points for dive trips to the Similan and Surin Islands, where the Andaman water is at its clearest. Out in the bay, Koh Yao Noi and Koh Yao Yai are still slow, village-style islands. People come to Phang Nga to cruise the bay among the karsts, dive the outer islands, and take the sea at an unhurried pace.",
