 "Thepprasit Night Market",
 "Thepprasit Night Market brings together street food, snacks, and shopping at friendly prices. It's a go-to evening stroll for locals and tourists alike.",
 "The Prima Residence",
 "The Privacy Beach Resort & Spa",
 "The province's best-known specialty — salted eggs packed in termite-mound clay from Chaiya, with a rich, sandy yolk. Eat them with rice congee or buy a batch to take home.",
 "The province's big island, with white-sand beaches, Kai Bae Beac",
 "The province's big island, with white-sand beaches, Kai Bae Beach, jungle waterfalls, and a wide range of places to stay from bungalows to resorts. The boat across from Ao Thammachat pier is short.",
 "The province's signature, grown everywhere. In winter the market",
 "The province's signature, grown everywhere. In winter the markets fill with sweet tamarind — buy it to take home as whole pods or processed snacks",
 "The province's signature souvenir — thin sheets of dough wrapped around colorful threads of spun sugar. You can buy it to take home at almost any shop in town.",
 "The province's top souvenir, sold all along the road as fresh pods, tamarind tossed with sugar, tamarind candy, and tangy spiced tamarind",
 "The pull of Hat Yai is its markets — Kim Yong and Santisuk sell imported snacks and goods, Khlong Hae is a floating market where vendors paddle boats selling southern Thai food, and Greenway–ASEAN is the night-market scene. For temple visits and views there's Hat Yai Municipal Park, where you ride a cable car up to pay respects at the giant Phra Buddha Mongkol Maharaj, the Brahma shrine, and a large Guanyin statue on the hill. Food is the real star here — Hat Yai fried chicken, morning dim sum, chicken rice, and a comfortable blend of Chinese and southern cooking. Come to Hat Yai to eat, shop, and use it as a base for exploring Songkhla and the lower south.",
 "The Quarter Ari by UHG",
 "The Quarter Onnut by UHG",
 "The Quarter Pai",
 "The Quarter Ramkhamhaeng by UHG",
 "The Quarter Ratchathewi by UHG",
 "The Quarter Residence Phayathai",
 "The Quart Ruamrudee by UHG",
 "The Rama Hotel",
 "There are three main beaches. Pattaya Beach has white sand and clear water, and it's where the boats land and where most of the lodging is. Sunrise Beach on the east side is for the morning sun, and Sunset Beach on the west is the quiet one. Down the middle of the island is Walking Street, lined with restaurants and bars. The highlight of Lipe is the snorkeling trip around the nearby islands — Koh Adang, Koh Rawi, Koh Hin Ngam (Stone Beach), and the Jabang reef — where the water is clear and the coral is beautiful. Honesty: Lipe is seasonal. During the monsoon from May to October the sea gets rough and a lot of the lodging and boats shut down. Things on the island cost more than on the mainland because everything has to be shipped in. Pack your trash out and don't touch the coral.",
 "There's a lot to do here in different styles. Head into the park for Haew Narok and Haew Suwat waterfalls, spot wildlife and hike the trails, stop for a tasting at GranMonte and PB Valley vineyards, wander European-themed villages like Palio and Primo Piazza, feed the sheep at a sheep farm, and linger over coffee at a mountain-view cafe. Khao Yai suits families, couples, cafe-hoppers, and nature lovers who just want to breathe some fresh air. Honesty: inside the park the roads wind and wildlife crosses, so drive slow and careful, and on long weekends traffic is heavy and rooms fill up fast, so book ahead.",
 "The Residence on Thonglor by UHG",
